 ## Subtopics
 
 ### NeRFVS
-NeRFVS is a method for indoor scene free view synthesis that uses a geometry scaffold from an off-the-shelf neural reconstruction method to guide NeRF optimization, reducing distortions and floaters in extrapolation [8667-nerfvs.md]. It enables NeRF to perform free navigation and extrapolation for indoor scenes by using a neural-reconstructed geometric scaffold to guide optimization, boosted by depth and variance constraints with dynamical adjustment based on view coverage [8667-nerfvs.md]. Unlike standard NeRF, which struggles with extrapolation and sparse views, NeRFVS minimizes per-pixel loss to avoid distortions, unlike SVS which suffers from noticeable artifacts [8667-nerfvs.md].
+NeRFVS is a method for indoor scene free view synthesis that uses a geometry scaffold from an off-the-shelf neural reconstruction method to guide NeRF optimization, reducing distortions and floaters in extrapolation [S1]. It enables NeRF to perform free navigation and extrapolation for indoor scenes by using a neural-reconstructed geometric scaffold to guide optimization, boosted by depth and variance constraints with dynamical adjustment based on view coverage [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF, which struggles with novel views significantly different from training views, NeRFVS reduces distortions and floaters by enforcing 3D consistent geometry and regularizing density/color variance [S1].
 
-*   **Geometry Scaffold:** A 3D geometric representation (e.g., point cloud or mesh) generated by an off-the-shelf neural reconstruction method using the input images and camera parameters [8667-nerfvs.md].
-*   **View Coverage Map:** An approximation tracking the number of training observations per region, stored as $V_i \in [1, N]^{H \times W \times 1}$, representing the count of views covering each pixel in the image plane [8667-nerfvs.md]. This map ignores emitting directions [8667-nerfvs.md].
